.RS 4
\fIA Minimalistic log print using termcapabities for native support for almost all terminal\&.\fP 
.RE
.PP
.SS "About"
As its name suggests, \fBminilog\fP is a tool dedicated to native logging based on termcapabilities \&. It adapts automatically to different terminals, thanks to its \fBsupport for termcapabilities\fP, and is often already present on most Unix systems\&.
.PP
Lightweight and easy to use, it has no external dependencies, which \fI\fBreduces the memory footprint\fP\fP when used\&.
.PP
By default, for fast display, standard output is not buffered, i\&.e\&. it is not timed\&. by the operating system, giving you instant display of messages\&. It can be quickly integrated into your workflow, as the project is built into a single file called a \fIshared object\fP\&.
.PP
It can be integrated into your code by creating a link to it\&.
.PP
.RS 4
[!IMPORTANT] For the moment, python support is under construction, and will be offered as a package using this shared object file\&.
.PP
.RE
.PP
.SS "How do I build it?"
To install or build it, we used the build manager called \fCMeson Build System\fP\&.
.PP
And here are the commands to type:
.PP
After cloning\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Enter to project\&. 
.PP
.nf
$ cd Minilog

.fi
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
start construction with meson 
.PP
.nf
$ meson setup build      # build the project
$ meson compile \-C build # compile project

.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
At the end of compilation, you'll have a \&.so file that can be integrated into your environment\&.
